  "markdown": "##### [cppreference.com](https://en.cppreference.com/index.html)\n\n[Create account](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Special:UserLogin&returnto=cpp%2Fcontainer%2Farray&type=signup)\n\n- [Log in](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Special:UserLogin&returnto=cpp%2Fcontainer%2Farray \"You are encouraged to log in; however, it is not mandatory [o]\")\n\n##### Namespaces\n\n- [Page](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array.html \"View the content page [c]\")\n- [Discussion](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Talk%253Acpp/container/array.html \"Discussion about the content page [t]\")\n\n##### Variants\n\n##### Views\n\n- [View](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array.html)\n- [Edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/container/array&action=edit \"You can edit this page. Please use the preview button before saving [e]\")\n- [History](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/container/array&action=history \"Past revisions of this page [h]\")\n\n##### Actions\n\n# std::array\n\nFrom cppreference.com\n\n< [cpp](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp.html \"cpp\") \u200e \\| [container](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container.html \"cpp/container\")\n\n[C++](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp.html \"cpp\")\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| [Compiler support](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/compiler_support.html \"cpp/compiler support\") |\n| [Freestanding and hosted](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/freestanding.html \"cpp/freestanding\") |\n| [Language](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language.html \"cpp/language\") |\n| [Standard library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/standard_library.html \"cpp/standard library\") |\n| [Standard library headers](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/headers.html \"cpp/header\") |\n| [Named requirements](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/iterator/concepts.html \"cpp/named req\") |\n| [Feature test macros](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/experimental/feature_test.html \"cpp/feature test\")(C++20) |\n| [Language support library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility.html#Language_support \"cpp/utility\") |\n| [Concepts library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/concepts.html \"cpp/concepts\")(C++20) |\n| [Diagnostics library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/error.html \"cpp/error\") |\n| [Memory management library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory.html \"cpp/memory\") |\n| [Metaprogramming library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/meta.html \"cpp/meta\")(C++11) |\n| [General utilities library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility.html \"cpp/utility\") |\n| [Containers library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container.html \"cpp/container\") |\n| [Iterators library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/iterator.html \"cpp/iterator\") |\n| [Ranges library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/ranges.html \"cpp/ranges\")(C++20) |\n| [Algorithms library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/algorithm.html \"cpp/algorithm\") |\n| [Strings library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string.html \"cpp/string\") |\n| [Text processing library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/text.html \"cpp/text\") |\n| [Numerics library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/numeric.html \"cpp/numeric\") |\n| [Date and time library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/chrono.html \"cpp/chrono\") |\n| [Input/output library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/io.html \"cpp/io\") |\n| [Filesystem library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/filesystem.html \"cpp/filesystem\")(C++17) |\n| [Concurrency support library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic.html \"cpp/thread\")(C++11) |\n| [Execution control library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/experimental/execution.html \"cpp/execution\")(C++26) |\n| [Technical specifications](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/experimental.html \"cpp/experimental\") |\n| [Symbols index](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/symbol_index.html \"cpp/symbol index\") |\n| [External libraries](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/links/libs.html \"cpp/links/libs\") |\n\n[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/navbar_content&action=edit)\n\n[Containers library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container.html \"cpp/container\")\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| [_node-handle_](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/node_handle.html \"cpp/container/node handle\")<br>(C++17) |\n| [Sequence](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container.html#Sequence_containers \"cpp/container\") |\n| **array**<br>(C++11) |\n| [vector](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/vector.html \"cpp/container/vector\") |\n| [vector<bool>](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/vector_bool.html \"cpp/container/vector bool\") |\n| [inplace\\_vector](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/inplace_vector.html \"cpp/container/inplace vector\")<br>(C++26) |\n| [hive](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/container/hive&action=edit&redlink=1 \"cpp/container/hive (page does not exist)\")<br>(C++26) |\n| [deque](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/deque.html \"cpp/container/deque\") |\n| [forward\\_list](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/forward_list.html \"cpp/container/forward list\")<br>(C++11) |\n| [list](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/list.html \"cpp/container/list\") |\n| [Associative](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container.html#Associative_containers \"cpp/container\") |\n| [set](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/set.html \"cpp/container/set\") |\n| [multiset](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/multiset.html \"cpp/container/multiset\") |\n| [map](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/map.html \"cpp/container/map\") |\n| [multimap](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/multimap.html \"cpp/container/multimap\") |\n| [Unordered associative](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container.html#Unordered_associative_containers \"cpp/container\") |\n| [unordered\\_set](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/unordered_set.html \"cpp/container/unordered set\")<br>(C++11) |\n| [unordered\\_multiset](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/unordered_multiset.html \"cpp/container/unordered multiset\")<br>(C++11) |\n| [unordered\\_map](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/unordered_map.html \"cpp/container/unordered map\")<br>(C++11) |\n| [unordered\\_multimap](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/unordered_multimap.html \"cpp/container/unordered multimap\")<br>(C++11) |\n| [Adaptors](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container.html#Container_adaptors \"cpp/container\") |\n| [stack](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/stack.html \"cpp/container/stack\") |\n| [queue](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/queue.html \"cpp/container/queue\") |\n| [priority\\_queue](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/priority_queue.html \"cpp/container/priority queue\") |\n| [flat\\_set](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/flat_set.html \"cpp/container/flat set\")<br>(C++23) |\n| [flat\\_multiset](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/flat_multiset.html \"cpp/container/flat multiset\")<br>(C++23) |\n| [flat\\_map](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/flat_map.html \"cpp/container/flat map\")<br>(C++23) |\n| [flat\\_multimap](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/flat_multimap.html \"cpp/container/flat multimap\")<br>(C++23) |\n| [Views](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container.html#Views \"cpp/container\") |\n| [span](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/span.html \"cpp/container/span\")<br>(C++20) |\n| [mdspan](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/mdspan.html \"cpp/container/mdspan\")<br>(C++23) |\n| Tables |\n| [Iterator invalidation](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container.html#Iterator_invalidation \"cpp/container\") |\n| [Member function table](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container.html#Member_function_table \"cpp/container\") |\n| [Non-member function table](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container.html#Non-member_function_table \"cpp/container\") |\n\n[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/navbar_content&action=edit)\n\n**`std::array`**\n\n|     |     |     |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [Member types](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array.html#Member_types \"cpp/container/array\") |\n| [Member functions](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array.html#Member_functions \"cpp/container/array\") |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| [Element access](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array.html#Element_access \"cpp/container/array\") |\n| [array::at](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/at.html \"cpp/container/array/at\") |\n| [array::operator\\[\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/operator_at.html \"cpp/container/array/operator at\")<br>`` |\n| [array::front](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/front.html \"cpp/container/array/front\") |\n| [array::back](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/back.html \"cpp/container/array/back\") |\n| [array::data](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/data.html \"cpp/container/array/data\") |\n| [Operations](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array.html#Operations \"cpp/container/array\") |\n| [array::fill](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/fill.html \"cpp/container/array/fill\") |\n| [array::swap](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/swap.html \"cpp/container/array/swap\") | | |     |\n| --- |\n| [Iterators](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array.html#Iterators \"cpp/container/array\") |\n| [array::beginarray::cbegin](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/begin.html \"cpp/container/array/begin\") |\n| [array::endarray::cend](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/end.html \"cpp/container/array/end\") |\n| [array::rbeginarray::crbegin](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/rbegin.html \"cpp/container/array/rbegin\")<br>`` |\n| [array::rendarray::crend](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/rend.html \"cpp/container/array/rend\") | | |     |\n| --- |\n| [Capacity](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array.html#Capacity \"cpp/container/array\") |\n| [array::empty](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/empty.html \"cpp/container/array/empty\") |\n| [array::size](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/size.html \"cpp/container/array/size\") |\n| [array::max\\_size](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/max_size.html \"cpp/container/array/max size\") |\n|  |\n|  |\n|  |\n|  |\n|  | |\n| [Non-member functions](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array.html#Non-member_functions \"cpp/container/array\") |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| [operator==operator<=>](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/operator_cmp.html \"cpp/container/array/operator cmp\")<br>(C++20) |\n| [get(std::array)](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/get.html \"cpp/container/array/get\") |\n| [swap(std::array)](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/swap2.html \"cpp/container/array/swap2\") |\n| [to\\_array](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/to_array.html \"cpp/container/array/to array\")<br>(C++20) | | |     |\n| --- |\n| [operator\\|=operator<operator>operator<=operator>=](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/operator_cmp.html \"cpp/container/array/operator cmp\")<br>(until C++20)(until C++20)(until C++20)(until C++20)(until C++20) | |\n| [Helper classes](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array.html#Helper_classes \"cpp/container/array\") |\n| [tuple\\_size<std::array>](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/tuple_size.html \"cpp/container/array/tuple size\") |\n| [tuple\\_element<std::array>](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/tuple_element.html \"cpp/container/array/tuple element\") |\n| [Deduction guides](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/deduction_guides.html \"cpp/container/array/deduction guides\")(C++17) |\n\n[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/array/navbar_content&action=edit)\n\n|     |     |     |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Defined in header `<array>` |  |  |\n| template<<br>class T,<br>[std::size\\_t](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/size_t.html) N<br>>struct array; |  | (since C++11) |\n|  |  |  |\n\n`std::array` is a container that encapsulates fixed size arrays.\n\nThis container is an aggregate type with the same semantics as a struct holding a [C-style array](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/array.html \"cpp/language/array\") T\\[N\\] as its only non-static data member. Unlike a C-style array, it doesn't decay to T\\* automatically. As an aggregate type, it can be initialized with [aggregate-initialization](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/aggregate_initialization.html \"cpp/language/aggregate initialization\") given at most `N` initializers that are convertible to `T`: std::array<int, 3> a ={1, 2, 3};.\n\nThe struct combines the performance and accessibility of a C-style array with the benefits of a standard container, such as knowing its own size, supporting assignment, random access iterators, etc.\n\n`std::array` satisfies the requirements of [Container](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/Container.html \"cpp/named req/Container\") and [ReversibleContainer](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/ReversibleContainer.html \"cpp/named req/ReversibleContainer\") except that default-constructed array is not empty and that the complexity of swapping is linear, satisfies the requirements of [ContiguousContainer](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/ContiguousContainer.html \"cpp/named req/ContiguousContainer\"),(since C++17) and partially satisfies the requirements of [SequenceContainer](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/SequenceContainer.html \"cpp/named req/SequenceContainer\").\n\nThere is a special case for a zero-length array (`N == 0`). In that case, array.begin()== array.end(), which is some unique value. The effect of calling front() or back() on a zero-sized array is undefined.\n\nAn array can also be used as a tuple of `N` elements of the same type.\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| ## Contents<br>- [1Iterator invalidation](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array.html#Iterator_invalidation)<br>- [2Template parameters](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array.html#Template_parameters)<br>- [3Member types](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array.html#Member_types)<br>- [4Member functions](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array.html#Member_functions)<br>  - [4.1Implicitly-defined member functions](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array.html#Implicitly-defined_member_functions)<br>  - [4.2Element access](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array.html#Element_access)<br>  - [4.3Iterators](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array.html#Iterators)<br>  - [4.4Capacity](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array.html#Capacity)<br>  - [4.5Operations](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array.html#Operations)<br>- [5Non-member functions](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array.html#Non-member_functions)<br>- [6Helper classes](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array.html#Helper_classes)<br>- [7Deduction guides](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array.html#Deduction_guides)<br>- [8Example](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array.html#Example)<br>- [9See also](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array.html#See_also) |\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/container/array&action=edit&section=1 \"Edit section: Iterator invalidation\")\\]Iterator invalidation\n\nAs a rule, iterators to an array are never invalidated throughout the lifetime of the array. One should take note, however, that during [swap](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/swap.html \"cpp/container/array/swap\"), the iterator will continue to point to the same array element, and will thus change its value.\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/container/array&action=edit&section=2 \"Edit section: Template parameters\")\\]Template parameters\n\n|     |     |     |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| T | - | element type Must be [MoveConstructible](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/MoveConstructible.html \"cpp/named req/MoveConstructible\") and [MoveAssignable](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/MoveAssignable.html \"cpp/named req/MoveAssignable\"). |\n| N | - | the number of elements in the array or \u200b0\u200b. |\n\n|     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n|  | This section is incomplete<br>Reason: Complete the descriptions of template parameters. |\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/container/array&action=edit&section=3 \"Edit section: Member types\")\\]Member types\n\n|     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n| Member type | Definition |\n| `value_type` | `T`[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/dsc_value_type&action=edit) |\n| `size_type` | [std::size\\_t](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/size_t.html \"cpp/types/size t\")[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/dsc_size_type&action=edit) |\n| `difference_type` | [std::ptrdiff\\_t](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/ptrdiff_t.html \"cpp/types/ptrdiff t\")[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/dsc_difference_type&action=edit) |\n| `reference` | value\\_type&[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/dsc_reference&action=edit) |\n| `const_reference` | const value\\_type&[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/dsc_const_reference&action=edit) |\n| `pointer` | value\\_type\\*[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/dsc_pointer&action=edit) |\n| `const_pointer` | const value\\_type\\*[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/dsc_const_pointer&action=edit) |\n| `iterator` | |     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n| [LegacyRandomAccessIterator](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/RandomAccessIterator.html \"cpp/named req/RandomAccessIterator\") and [LegacyContiguousIterator](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/ContiguousIterator.html \"cpp/named req/ContiguousIterator\") to `value_type` | (until C++17) |\n| [LegacyRandomAccessIterator](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/RandomAccessIterator.html \"cpp/named req/RandomAccessIterator\") and [LegacyContiguousIterator](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/ContiguousIterator.html \"cpp/named req/ContiguousIterator\") that is a [LiteralType](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/LiteralType.html \"cpp/named req/LiteralType\") to `value_type` | (since C++17)<br>(until C++20) |\n| [LegacyRandomAccessIterator](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/RandomAccessIterator.html \"cpp/named req/RandomAccessIterator\"), [`contiguous_iterator`](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/iterator/contiguous_iterator.html \"cpp/iterator/contiguous iterator\"), and [ConstexprIterator](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/ConstexprIterator.html \"cpp/named req/ConstexprIterator\") to `value_type` | (since C++20) |\n\n[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/dsc_iterator&action=edit) |\n| `const_iterator` | |     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n| [LegacyRandomAccessIterator](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/RandomAccessIterator.html \"cpp/named req/RandomAccessIterator\") and [LegacyContiguousIterator](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/ContiguousIterator.html \"cpp/named req/ContiguousIterator\") to const value\\_type | (until C++17) |\n| [LegacyRandomAccessIterator](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/RandomAccessIterator.html \"cpp/named req/RandomAccessIterator\") and [LegacyContiguousIterator](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/ContiguousIterator.html \"cpp/named req/ContiguousIterator\") that is a [LiteralType](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/LiteralType.html \"cpp/named req/LiteralType\") to const value\\_type | (since C++17)<br>(until C++20) |\n| [LegacyRandomAccessIterator](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/RandomAccessIterator.html \"cpp/named req/RandomAccessIterator\"), [`contiguous_iterator`](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/iterator/contiguous_iterator.html \"cpp/iterator/contiguous iterator\"), and [ConstexprIterator](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/ConstexprIterator.html \"cpp/named req/ConstexprIterator\") to const value\\_type | (since C++20) |\n\n[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/dsc_const_iterator&action=edit) |\n| `reverse_iterator` | [std::reverse\\_iterator](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/iterator/reverse_iterator.html) <iterator>[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/dsc_reverse_iterator&action=edit) |\n| `const_reverse_iterator` | [std::reverse\\_iterator](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/iterator/reverse_iterator.html) <const\\_iterator>[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/dsc_const_reverse_iterator&action=edit) |\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/container/array&action=edit&section=4 \"Edit section: Member functions\")\\]Member functions\n\n|     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n| ##### Implicitly-defined member functions |\n| (constructor)<br>(implicitly declared) | initializes the array following the rules of [aggregate initialization](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/aggregate_initialization.html \"cpp/language/aggregate initialization\") (note that default initialization may result in indeterminate values for non-class `T`) <br>(public member function) |\n| (destructor)<br>(implicitly declared) | destroys every element of the array <br>(public member function) |\n| operator=<br>(implicitly declared) | overwrites every element of the array with the corresponding element of another array <br>(public member function) |\n| ##### Element access |\n| [at](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/at.html \"cpp/container/array/at\") | access specified element with bounds checking <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/dsc_at&action=edit) |\n| [operator\\[\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/operator_at.html \"cpp/container/array/operator at\") | access specified element <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/dsc_operator_at&action=edit) |\n| [front](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/front.html \"cpp/container/array/front\") | access the first element <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/dsc_front&action=edit) |\n| [back](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/back.html \"cpp/container/array/back\") | access the last element <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/dsc_back&action=edit) |\n| [data](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/data.html \"cpp/container/array/data\") | direct access to the underlying contiguous storage <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/dsc_data&action=edit) |\n| ##### Iterators |\n| [begincbegin](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/begin.html \"cpp/container/array/begin\") | returns an iterator to the beginning <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/dsc_begin&action=edit) |\n| [endcend](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/end.html \"cpp/container/array/end\") | returns an iterator to the end <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/dsc_end&action=edit) |\n| [rbegincrbegin](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/rbegin.html \"cpp/container/array/rbegin\") | returns a reverse iterator to the beginning <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/dsc_rbegin&action=edit) |\n| [rendcrend](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/rend.html \"cpp/container/array/rend\") | returns a reverse iterator to the end <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/dsc_rend&action=edit) |\n| ##### Capacity |\n| [empty](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/empty.html \"cpp/container/array/empty\") | checks whether the container is empty <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/dsc_empty&action=edit) |\n| [size](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/size.html \"cpp/container/array/size\") | returns the number of elements <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/dsc_size&action=edit) |\n| [max\\_size](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/max_size.html \"cpp/container/array/max size\") | returns the maximum possible number of elements <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/dsc_max_size&action=edit) |\n| ##### Operations |\n| [fill](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/fill.html \"cpp/container/array/fill\") | fill the container with specified value <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/dsc_fill&action=edit) |\n| [swap](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/swap.html \"cpp/container/array/swap\") | swaps the contents <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/dsc_swap&action=edit) |\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/container/array&action=edit&section=5 \"Edit section: Non-member functions\")\\]Non-member functions\n\n|     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n| [operator==operator!=operator<operator<=operator>operator>=operator<=>](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/operator_cmp.html \"cpp/container/array/operator cmp\")<br>(C++11)(C++11)(removed in C++20)(C++11)(removed in C++20)(C++11)(removed in C++20)(C++11)(removed in C++20)(C++11)(removed in C++20)(C++20) | lexicographically compares the values of two `array`s <br>(function template)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/dsc_operator_cmp&action=edit) |\n| [get(std::array)](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/get.html \"cpp/container/array/get\")<br>(C++11) | accesses an element of an `array`<br>(function template)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/array/dsc_get&action=edit) |\n| [std::swap(std::array)](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/swap2.html \"cpp/container/array/swap2\")<br>(C++11) | specializes the [std::swap](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/swap.html \"cpp/algorithm/swap\") algorithm <br>(function template)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/dsc_swap2&action=edit) |\n| [to\\_array](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/to_array.html \"cpp/container/array/to array\")<br>(C++20) | creates a `std::array` object from a built-in array <br>(function template)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/array/dsc_to_array&action=edit) |\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/container/array&action=edit&section=6 \"Edit section: Helper classes\")\\]Helper classes\n\n|     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n| [std::tuple\\_size<std::array>](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/tuple_size.html \"cpp/container/array/tuple size\")<br>(C++11) | obtains the size of an `array`<br>(class template specialization)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/array/dsc_tuple_size&action=edit) |\n| [std::tuple\\_element<std::array>](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/tuple_element.html \"cpp/container/array/tuple element\")<br>(C++11) | obtains the type of the elements of `array`<br>(class template specialization)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/array/dsc_tuple_element&action=edit) |\n\n|     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n| ### [Deduction guides](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/deduction_guides.html \"cpp/container/array/deduction guides\") | (since C++17) |\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/container/array&action=edit&section=8 \"Edit section: Example\")\\]Example\n\nRun this code\n\n```\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <array>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <iterator>\n#include <string>\n\nint main()\n{\n    // Construction uses aggregate initialization\n    std::array<int, 3> a1{{1, 2, 3}}; // Double-braces required in C++11 prior to\n                                      // the CWG 1270 revision (not needed in C++11\n                                      // after the revision and in C++14 and beyond)\n\n    std::array<int, 3> a2 = {1, 2, 3}; // Double braces never required after =\n\n    // Container operations are supported\n    std::sort(a1.begin(), a1.end());\n    std::ranges::reverse_copy(a2, std::ostream_iterator<int>(std::cout, \" \"));\n    std::cout << '\\n';\n\n    // Ranged for loop is supported\n    std::array<std::string, 2> a3{\"E\", \"\\u018E\"};\n    for (const auto& s : a3)\n        std::cout << s << ' ';\n    std::cout << '\\n';\n\n    // Deduction guide for array creation (since C++17)\n    [[maybe_unused]] std::array a4{3.0, 1.0, 4.0}; // std::array<double, 3>\n\n    // Behavior of unspecified elements is the same as with built-in arrays\n    [[maybe_unused]] std::array<int, 2> a5; // No list init, a5[0] and a5[1]\n                                            // are default initialized\n    [[maybe_unused]] std::array<int, 2> a6{}; // List init, both elements are value\n                                              // initialized, a6[0] = a6[1] = 0\n    [[maybe_unused]] std::array<int, 2> a7{1}; // List init, unspecified element is value\n                                               // initialized, a7[0] = 1, a7[1] = 0\n}\n```\n\nOutput:\n\n```\n3 2 1\nE \u018e\n```\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/container/array&action=edit&section=9 \"Edit section: See also\")\\]See also\n\n|     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n| [inplace\\_vector](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/inplace_vector.html \"cpp/container/inplace vector\")<br>(C++26) | resizable, fixed capacity, inplace contiguous array <br>(class template)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/dsc_inplace_vector&action=edit) |\n| [vector](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/vector.html \"cpp/container/vector\") | resizable contiguous array <br>(class template)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/dsc_vector&action=edit) |\n| [deque](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/deque.html \"cpp/container/deque\") | double-ended queue <br>(class template)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/container/dsc_deque&action=edit) |\n| [make\\_array](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/experimental/make_array.html \"cpp/experimental/make array\")<br>(library fundamentals TS v2) | creates a **std::array** object whose size and optionally element type are deduced from the arguments <br>(function template)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/experimental/dsc_make_array&action=edit) |\n\nRetrieved from \" [https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/container/array&oldid=174050](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/container/array&oldid=174050)\"\n\n[Category](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Special:Categories \"Special:Categories\"):\n\n- [Todo with reason](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Category%253ATodo_with_reason.html \"Category:Todo with reason\")\n\n##### Navigation\n\n- [Support us](http://www.cppreference.com/support)\n- [Recent changes](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Special:RecentChanges \"A list of recent changes in the wiki [r]\")\n- [FAQ](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Cppreference%253AAbout.html)\n- [Offline version](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Cppreference%253AArchives.html)\n\n##### Toolbox\n\n- [What links here](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Special:WhatLinksHere/cpp/container/array \"A list of all wiki pages that link here [j]\")\n- [Related changes](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Special:RecentChangesLinked/cpp/container/array \"Recent changes in pages linked from this page [k]\")\n- [Upload file](http://upload.cppreference.com/w/Special:Upload \"Upload files [u]\")\n- [Special pages](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Special:SpecialPages \"A list of all special pages [q]\")\n- [Printable version](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/container/array&printable=yes \"Printable version of this page [p]\")\n- [Permanent link](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/container/array&oldid=174050 \"Permanent link to this revision of the page\")\n- [Page information](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/container/array&action=info)\n\n- In other languages\n\n- [Deutsch](http://de.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array \"cpp/container/array\")\n- [Espa\u00f1ol](http://es.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array \"cpp/container/array\")\n- [Fran\u00e7ais](http://fr.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array \"cpp/container/array\")\n- [Italiano](http://it.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array \"cpp/container/array\")\n- [\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e](http://ja.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array \"cpp/container/array\")\n- [Polski](http://pl.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array \"cpp/container/array\")\n- [Portugu\u00eas](http://pt.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array \"cpp/container/array\")\n- [\u0420\u0443\u0441\u0441\u043a\u0438\u0439](http://ru.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array \"cpp/container/array\")\n- [\u4e2d\u6587](http://zh.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array \"cpp/container/array\")\n\n- This page was last modified on 2 August 2024, at 22:20.\n\n- [Privacy policy](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Cppreference%253APrivacy_policy.html \"Cppreference:Privacy policy\")\n- [About cppreference.com](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Cppreference%253AAbout.html \"Cppreference:About\")\n- [Disclaimers](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Cppreference%253AGeneral_disclaimer.html \"Cppreference:General disclaimer\")\n\n- [![Powered by MediaWiki](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/skins/common/images/poweredby_mediawiki_88x31.png)](https://www.mediawiki.org/)[![Powered by GeSHi](https://upload.cppreference.com/mwiki/images/2/2b/powered_by_geshi_88x31.png)](http://qbnz.com/highlighter/)[![Hosted by Tiger Technologies](https://upload.cppreference.com/mwiki/images/9/94/powered_by_tigertech_88x31.png)](http://www.tigertech.net/referral/cppreference.com)",
